Ninaro - HELP - Ninaro - HELP - Ninaro - HELP - Ninaro -

~Ninaro
Ninaro stands for N-in-a-row, which means that the connect
four game has been extended to connect any number on any
sized grid. Logically however a minimum of 3x3x3 applies.

~Player's Keys
Each player has a set of keys, consisting of Left,Right,Up,
Down,Select and Cancel. The table below shows these keys.

~Table of Player Keys
        Player One      Player Two
Left        A           Keypad 4
Right       D           Keypad 6
Up          W           Keypad 8
Down        S           Keypad 2
Select      E           Enter
Cancel      Q           Backspace

The keypad keys can be used as either the grey arrow keys
or the numbered keys on the numerical keypad for which
numlock must be off.

~What The Keys Do.
Depending on where you are in the program, the keys do
different things, though they are quite similar. The
table below shows the functionality of the keys at each
location on the program.

~Table of Key Functionality
        Playing A Game      Using Menu      Using Dialogs
Left    Token Left          Left a Menu     Left an item
Right   Token Right         Right a Menu    Right an item
Up      Calls the menu      Up an item      Up a group
Down    Drops Token         Down an item    Down a group
Select  Drops Token         Select Item     Select Button-
                                            OK,Reset,Cancel
Cancel  Calls the menu      Cancel Menu     Cancels Dialog

~The Menus.
The menus are the key way in Ninaro of changing things. The
menu is accessable at almost anytime by pressing ESC, M for
menu, or your appropriate player key.

~The Dialogs
Dialogs help you choose from a group of options. In the
dialogs C cancels, R resets and O ok's. Pressing Select
at any time while in the dialog results on the hilited
button (OK,Reset,Cancel) being used, while pressing cancel
cancels the dialog.
